      "title": "My day",
      "canDo": "Describe a basic daily routine and say when things happen",
      "tip": {
        "title": "The conjugated verb stays in position two",
        "body": "A German statement keeps its conjugated verb in the second position. You can begin with the person: **Ich frühstücke morgens.** If you begin with the time, the person moves after the verb: **Morgens frühstücke ich.** English normally keeps the subject before the verb in both versions.\n\nSome common routine verbs change their stem: **du fährst** and **du liest**. Learn **ich stehe auf** as a useful routine chunk for “I get up”; the small word **auf** goes at the end here.",
        "examples": [
          { "target": "Morgens frühstücke ich.", "source": "I eat breakfast in the morning." },
          { "target": "Abends liest sie.", "source": "She reads in the evening." },
          { "target": "Ich stehe früh auf.", "source": "I get up early." }
        ]
      },
