    {
      "id": "u14",
      "title": "My home",
      "canDo": "Describe rooms, furniture, and where things are in a home",
      "tip": {
        "title": "Use es gibt for there is and there are",
        "body": "German uses **es gibt** for both English “there is” and “there are”: **Es gibt ein Bad** and **Es gibt zwei Zimmer**. The thing that exists is a direct object, so a masculine noun uses **einen**: **Es gibt einen Schrank.**\n\nUse **hier** for “here” and **dort** for “there.” They can begin the sentence, but the conjugated verb still comes second: **Hier ist die Küche.**",
        "examples": [
